    "notes": [
      {
        "category": "summary",
        "text": "An update is available for libcupsfilters.\nThis update affects Rocky Linux 10.\nA Common Vulnerability Scoring System (CVSS) base score, which gives a detailed severity rating, is available for each vulnerability from the CVE list",
        "title": "Topic"
      },
      {
        "category": "description",
        "text": "Libcupsfilters provides a library, which implements common functions used in cups-browsed daemon and printing filters, and additional files as banner templates and character sets. The filters are used in CUPS daemon and in printer applications.\n\nSecurity Fix(es):\n\n* libcupsfilters: cups-filters: libcupsfilters: CPU exhaustion via infinite loop in cfIEEE1284NormalizeMakeModel() (CVE-2026-64611)\n\n* libcupsfilters: cups-filters: libcupsfilters: CUPS image filter process abort via malformed PNG (CVE-2026-64612)\n\nFor more details about the security issue(s), including the impact, a CVSS score, acknowledgments, and other related information, refer to the CVE page(s) listed in the References section.\n\nThis advisory is provided by Ctrl IQ, Inc for Rocky Linux systems. For more information about CIQ security practices, visit https://ciq.com/security.",
        "title": "Description"
      },
      {
